# Deployment-readiness pass (docs/evaluation.md, 2026-08-08): the build
# context had no .dockerignore, so `COPY . .` was pulling in the whole
# repo -- .git history, local dev-DB backup tarballs, every cache
# directory -- which is why a from-scratch build's final `chown -R /app`
# step took several minutes copying/chowning files the image never needs.
# None of this belongs in the image; excluding it here is a straight size
# and build-time win, not a behavior change.
.git/
.github/
backups/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.coverage
htmlcov/
loadtest/results/
docs/
tests/
*.md
.env
.env.example
